  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Guatemala (01-Jul-2018-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guatemala, Malaria, Ministry of Health and Social Assistance of the Republic of Guatemala (MSPAS)This program has the following goals: Interrupt autoctonous malaria transmission by Plasmodium Vivax by year 2020.  Maintain interruption of transmission by Plasmodium falciparum. The objectives of this program are: Strengthen prevention, surveillance, diagnosis and integrated vector management in 8 districts in control phase.  Acheive consolidation of gains met for districts with major incidence of malaria cases.  Strengthen local capacity for surveillance, alert and response activities to outbreaks and epidemics.  Improve governance of the pre elimination program of malaria and administrative and financial management of the grant in Guatemala</narrative>
  </description>
